{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Duda'im [mandrakes].</b> The translator [Onkelos] says יברוחין [mandrakes], and so they are called in the language of Ishmael, and they have a good fragrance, as it is written: הדודאים נתנו ריח (Song of Songs 7:14), and they are in the shape of a human, for they have the form of a head and hands. As for me, I do not know why they would help for conception, since their nature is cold."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:21.450540146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}